  "title": "# Configurable max-agents cap + queue (Brett, Nov 1 early) Read CLAUDE.md, _claude/shared/rules/RUL…",
  "asked": "# Configurable max-agents cap + queue (Brett, Nov 1 early) Read CLAUDE.md, _claude/shared/rules/RULES.md, _claude/persona.md. Opus, one session. Git login works: plain `git push`. Server: 16 GB RAM (a 4 GB swap file is being added), headless Claude sessions ~300-400 MB idle, 1-2 GB while running tests/builds. Brett wants a CONFIGURABLE cap on how many agents/builds run at once; extras wait in line. 1. deploy/claude-headless.sh (and anything else that launches `claude -p`: swarm agents, orchestrator runs): before starting, check running headless sessions; if at the cap, register in a queue (FIFO with priority: Boss/urgent first) and start automatically when a slot frees. Sessions that are 'finished, waiting to close' do not count; close them automatically after they finish (keep the log). 2. Settings (one place, hot-reloaded, shown in the console's Settings and the Breakroom/HR panel settings): max running agents (default 6), max running tests/builds at once (default 3, a lock around heavy test/build steps: pnpm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright), memory guard (don't start a new one if available memory < X GB, default 2), priority rules. 3. Console: show slots used / cap in the activity banner's one-line summary, the queue (position, waiting since) in the Builds page, with move up / cancel. 4. The swarm (agent-swarm plugin) respects the same cap; HR 'on duty' agents beyond the cap show 'waiting for a desk'. 5. Systems-check item: warns when memory guard trips often or swap is in use for long. Note: axHub's vps.build_start calls deploy/claude-headless.sh, so the queue applies to it automatically; make build_start's output say 'queued at position N' when queued (that string comes from the script's stdout). Tests: cap, queue order, priority, auto-start on free slot, finished sessions not counted + auto-closed, memory guard, settings hot reload. Full local test block from .github/workflows/android.yml + theme/controls/lifecycle checks. Phone + desktop screenshots to UI Review via framework/cli/shot.mjs, group 'Agent cap - Nov 1'. Merge origin/main first (banner-fix and the swarm HR builds may touch nearby files). Commit, fetch+merge origin/main, retest, `git push origin HEAD:main` (never force). Report at _claude/builds/reports/agent-cap.md. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, patches-web, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault).",
